# failure_unhandled_propagate — NEGATIVE test. A fallible call declares `catch`
# but main never `branch ifError`s on it, so the error case is unhandled
# (README §17 #35). The linter must flag this — a hidden failure is exactly what
# the language forbids. This is a load-bearing test of the unhandled-error check.
#
# Correctness observation (verified): `eavc check` reports
#   WARNING SS3501: fallible call 'writeLine' has a catch but no `branch ifError`
# (advisory tier, so it still runs by default; `run --strict` promotes it to a
# blocking error). Proves the hidden-failure checker fires.
# Expected: flagged with SS3501.

FailureUnhandledPropagate is project
FailureUnhandledPropagate module examplesFailureUnhandledPropagate
FailureUnhandledPropagate target console
FailureUnhandledPropagate entry main

examplesFailureUnhandledPropagate is module
examplesFailureUnhandledPropagate path examples.failureUnhandledPropagate
examplesFailureUnhandledPropagate exports main
examplesFailureUnhandledPropagate purpose "Leave a fallible call's error case unhandled"
examplesFailureUnhandledPropagate invariant "The catch has no matching ifError on purpose"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

ConsoleWriteError is error
ConsoleWriteError purpose "Represent failures from console output operations"

ConsoleWriteFailed is errorCase
ConsoleWriteFailed of ConsoleWriteError
ConsoleWriteFailed payload Int32
ConsoleWriteFailed purpose "A failed stdout write with a status payload"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Perform a fallible write but never handle its error case"
main invariant "Deliberately omits branch ifError to trip the checker"
main let lineText immutable String "unhandled fallible write"
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do writeLine
main return okCode

writeLine is call
writeLine in main
writeLine invokes console.writeLine
writeLine arg text String lineText
writeLine catch writeError ConsoleWriteError
